I enter the museum.
There is no wetness in this lobby.
I close my umbrella and shake the water off it.
A few minutes ago, I was outside in the heavy rain.
I walk to the ticket counter.
A clerk is sitting there.
He smiles at me happily.
"Do you want a ticket?" he asks.
"Yes, I need one ticket," I reply.
I give him fifty rupees.
He gives me a ticket and a book.
"What is that?" I ask.
"That is a brochure about this museum," he says.
"Where is the main exhibit hall?" I ask.
"That hall is on the ground floor," he replies.
I say thank you to him.
Then I open that brochure.
I walk to the main hall on the ground floor.
